{
  "answer": "Ethical issues raised by the abstract include: (1) resource and environmental cost due to the reported scale: \"largest existing language model as of today (989 trillion parameters, dataset of 968 Pb)\"; (2) data provenance and consent, because training used \"not only freely available Web content, but also Web archives and publicly-accessible EPub versions of all the books of the commercial Amazonia bookshop web storefront,\" raising questions about copyright, licensing, and lawful access to commercial book content; (3) crowdworker welfare, because the best results were obtained using \"reinforcement learning with human feedback (RLHF) coming from crowdworkers\" but the abstract discloses no pay, consent, or support conditions; and (4) access and accountability, because \"BigBlue is available through an API,\" which may limit independent auditing and concentrate control. The abstract itself does not discuss ethical review, opt-out mechanisms, or mitigation of these risks.",
